    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_e977adf2cb9b4e5b7b69cb520bb668efd80b7f4ed025cd4c81717d054144cb5c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Li's positive-operator factorization requires the local-factor multiplier to preserve a Hardy subspace, equivalently for its adjoint to be inner; unit critical-line modulus is insufficient because the arithmetic ratios are unbounded in the relevant half-plane. The resulting unrestricted inequality is false, while Weil's actual criterion restores two vanishing moments and motivates a support-dependent finite-place conjecture.",
